jordanForm -- Jordan canonical form
***********************************

  * Usage: 
        jordanForm(A)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a square matrix.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Tolerance => ..., default value .001, numerical tolerance.
  * Outputs:
      * chBasMatr, the matrix  that transforms A in Jordan form.
      * sepEigen, the generalized eigenvectors.
      * eigNrep, the eigenvalues of the matrix A.
      * algMult, the algebraic multiplicity of each eigenvalue.
      * jorFor, the Jordan form of A.

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = matrix{{1,2},{-1,3}}                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | 1  2 |                                                                |
|     | -1 3 |                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|              2       2                                                      |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (pCh,sepEigs,peigs,palgm,JF) = jordanForm(A)                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = (| .816497           .816497           |, {| .816497           |, |     |
|      | .408248+.408248ii .408248-.408248ii |   | .408248+.408248ii |  |     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     .816497           |}, {2+ii, 2-ii}, {1, 1}, | 2+ii 0    |)              |
|     .408248-.408248ii |                         | 0    2-ii |               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

the procedure involves computation over inexact field and hence the results may
be not reliable.

